    <briefdescription>
<para>GPU-accelerated boundary-patch force and moment calculator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Registered in OpenFOAM&apos;s runtime selection table under the type name <computeroutput>neoForces</computeroutput>. Can be driven directly from <computeroutput>controlDict:</computeroutput> <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">functions</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>wallForces</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="classNeoFOAM_1_1Forces_1a304be0e6fcd89e0dcdb722b003d78f5c" kindref="member">type</ref><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>neoForces;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>libs<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>(<ref refid="namespaceNeoFOAM" kindref="compound">NeoFOAM</ref>);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>patches<sp/><sp/><sp/>(fixedWalls);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>pName<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>uName<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>U;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>rhoInf<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>1.0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>pRef<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>0.0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>CofR<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>(0<sp/>0<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>GPU I/O strategy</title><para><ref refid="classNeoFOAM_1_1Forces_1ad9ae38e7170e3b4a121fb1a0a46d5e2e" kindref="member">execute()</ref> runs a <computeroutput>parallelFor</computeroutput> kernel over the boundary patch faces using <computeroutput>NeoN::atomic_add</computeroutput> into a 6-element device buffer. Only those 6 scalars (96 bytes) are copied to host — the full pressure field is never transferred. <ref refid="classNeoFOAM_1_1Forces_1ab2664062354c5f34078252d7f22dc4ca" kindref="member">write()</ref> appends one row each to <computeroutput>postProcessing/</computeroutput> &lt;name&gt;/&lt;startTime&gt;/force.dat and <computeroutput>postProcessing/</computeroutput> &lt;name&gt;/&lt;startTime&gt;/moment.dat.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>MPI parallel execution is not supported; a FatalError is raised in <ref refid="classNeoFOAM_1_1Forces_1ad9ae38e7170e3b4a121fb1a0a46d5e2e" kindref="member">execute()</ref> if Pstream::parRun() is true. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
